WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.470
(audience clapping)
- All right everybody,

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:03.480
I always like to finish up
with something uplifting.

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.021
Here's today's #What I'm Liking.

00:00:05.021 --> 00:00:08.160
(lively upbeat music)
(audience clapping)

00:00:08.160 --> 00:00:10.440
Back in our first season,
Kaley Cuoco introduced me

00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:13.020
to her friend and manager,
Andrea Pett-Joseph.

00:00:13.020 --> 00:00:15.690
Andrea's son, Brandon was
born with a super rare disease

00:00:15.690 --> 00:00:18.750
that makes his skin as
fragile as butterfly wings.

00:00:18.750 --> 00:00:21.480
He constantly suffers wounds and blisters.

00:00:21.480 --> 00:00:23.010
Andrea does everything she can

00:00:23.010 --> 00:00:25.830
to give Brandon a normal
and comfortable life,

00:00:25.830 --> 00:00:28.020
but she's also on a
mission to find a cure,

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.120
so no other child has to go through this.

00:00:30.120 --> 00:00:31.560
We have Andrea on the line right now.

00:00:31.560 --> 00:00:32.792
So say hi to Andrea everybody.

00:00:32.792 --> 00:00:35.970
(audience applauds)
Hi, Andrea.

00:00:35.970 --> 00:00:37.110
- Hello.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.670
- Hello, it's good to see you again.

00:00:38.670 --> 00:00:40.140
So it's been three years now.

00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.670
How's Brandon doing?

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:44.730
- It has been three years, which is crazy.

00:00:44.730 --> 00:00:47.040
You know, as you know, he's got EB,

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:49.350
and that has its set of challenges.

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:53.220
So there's been health
issues on a daily basis.

00:00:53.220 --> 00:00:56.670
And he's also had some great milestones

00:00:56.670 --> 00:00:57.930
since we last saw you.

00:00:57.930 --> 00:00:59.760
He graduated from high school.

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:00.593
- [Kelly] Oh, wow.

00:01:00.593 --> 00:01:01.426
(audience applauds)

00:01:01.426 --> 00:01:04.352
- He started college at LMU.
- That's so awesome.

00:01:04.352 --> 00:01:05.927
Yeah, there he is. (laughs)

00:01:05.927 --> 00:01:09.690
But he remains positive
and hopeful, as do we.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:11.640
And we're just really, really proud of him

00:01:11.640 --> 00:01:12.835
and all his accomplishments.

00:01:12.835 --> 00:01:14.910
- Oh, me too, that's incredible,

00:01:14.910 --> 00:01:15.900
all the things that he's accomplished.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:18.300
So remind everybody though,
about your foundation,

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.980
the EB Medical Research Foundation.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:21.704
So like, how can they help?

00:01:21.704 --> 00:01:24.840
- Well, yeah, so we started
the foundation in L.A.

00:01:24.840 --> 00:01:28.050
when Brandon was born, and
our goal is to raise money

00:01:28.050 --> 00:01:30.720
and to raise awareness for EB.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:32.550
We fund numerous researchers

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:35.100
and universities who have projects.

00:01:35.100 --> 00:01:37.773
So that's sort of our main goal.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:40.620
Our biggest fundraiser is coming up,

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:43.950
which we're really excited
about, to be back in person.

00:01:43.950 --> 00:01:45.840
It's our Rock4EB! that we do.

00:01:45.840 --> 00:01:47.820
It's our sixth year of doing it.

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:51.090
And we've had Ed Sheeran
perform, Eddie Vedder,

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:55.021
Adam Sandler, Chris Cornell, Sting,

00:01:55.021 --> 00:01:57.750
and this year we've got Brandi Carlile,

00:01:57.750 --> 00:01:59.910
and Judd Apatow and Kevin Nealon,

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:02.373
so we're really excited
to be back in person.

00:02:03.450 --> 00:02:05.190
And we're selling tickets,

00:02:05.190 --> 00:02:07.320
and it's just a great, magical night,

00:02:07.320 --> 00:02:09.840
and everyone comes out for
the cause and the music

00:02:09.840 --> 00:02:11.100
and the great food,

00:02:11.100 --> 00:02:13.800
and it's a really incredible night

00:02:13.800 --> 00:02:16.290
for all of us to help raise
awareness and funds for EB.

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:17.643
So we're very excited about that.

00:02:17.643 --> 00:02:18.482
(audience applauds)

00:02:18.482 --> 00:02:20.640
- Man, congratulations on that.

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:23.820
To find out more about the EB
Medical Research Foundation

00:02:23.820 --> 00:02:26.070
and how you can help
the search for a cure,

00:02:26.070 --> 00:02:28.140
go to "The Kelly Clarkson
Show" Insta Story right now.

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:30.180
Thank you so much everybody,
and thank you, Andrea.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:31.904
I'm liking your post right now.

00:02:31.904 --> 00:02:33.828
(audience cheers)

00:02:33.828 --> 00:02:35.250
- [Andrea] Thank you.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:36.420
- Absolutely, and that's not all.

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:37.380
Our season-long partner,

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.730
Pilot Pen, makers of G2,

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:40.560
the Go-To Pen of "The
Kelly Clarkson Show,"

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:42.390
want to honor truly unstoppable people

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:43.223
just like you, ma'am.

00:02:43.223 --> 00:02:44.760
So, they're gonna be writing

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:46.740
the EB Medical Research Foundation a check

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:47.607
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:47.607 --> 00:02:49.708
(audience cheers)

00:02:49.708 --> 00:02:50.977
- Oh my god.

00:02:50.977 --> 00:02:52.320
Wow, thank you so-
- Yeah.

00:02:52.320 --> 00:02:53.417
- Oh, that's incredible.

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:55.110
Thank you, thank you all so much.

00:02:55.110 --> 00:02:57.308
That's really, really appreciated.

00:02:57.308 --> 00:02:58.330
(audience cheers)
- Absolutely, girl.

